    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="1002" n="994" xml:id="pg994"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12815: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-04T14:00:00+07:00">July 4, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 4—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>274. During courtesy call at Embassy today Generalissimo Chiang told me an attack
                    by Japan on Siberia is certain. He stated Japan will denounce neutrality pact
                    with Russia and simultaneously or shortly thereafter attack in Siberia. He
                    stated his source of information is very reliable and suggested I inform my
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
